From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-network: grant the resolved paths rpcd now checks
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

rpcd since 2026-07-19 (e37ed9d, taken with 0050) resolves symlinks in a
requested path and checks the session's permissions against the resolved
path as well. Two LuCI network views read through symlinks whose targets
were not granted:

- Bridge port options read /sys/class/net/<dev>/brport/<name>, which
  resolves below /sys/devices. The read failed and the view showed
  learning, unicast flooding and port isolation as "automatic (disabled)"
  whatever the real state.
- Diagnostics tests for /bin/ping6 and /bin/traceroute6 with stat. Both
  are links to busybox here, so the test failed and the IPv6 variants
  were not offered.

Grant read on the resolved bridge port paths and stat ("list") on
/bin/busybox. Running the tools is unaffected: rpcd does not resolve the
path it executes. Upstream LuCI has the same gap as of 2026-11-25
(master 8d1aecd021); 0055 carries its earlier fix for /proc paths.

diff --git a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
--- a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/rpcd/acl.d/luci-mod-network.json
@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@
 				"/proc/sys/net/ipv6/conf/*/hop_limit": [ "read" ],
 				"/usr/libexec/luci-peeraddr": [ "exec" ],
 				"/proc/sys/net/ipv[46]/conf/*": [ "read" ],
-				"/sys/class/net/*/brport/*": [ "read" ]
+				"/sys/class/net/*/brport/*": [ "read" ],
+				"/sys/devices/*/net/*/brport/*": [ "read" ]
 			},
 			"ubus": {
 				"file": [ "exec" ],
@@ -66,6 +67,7 @@
 		"description": "Grant access to network diagnostic tools",
 		"read": {
 			"file": {
+				"/bin/busybox": [ "list" ],
 				"/bin/ping": [ "exec" ],
 				"/bin/ping6": [ "exec", "list" ],
 				"/bin/traceroute": [ "exec" ],
